        "header": "1Introduction",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.00768/2609.00768v1/intro.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:Co-evolution under pure free exploration and DiagEvo. (a) Pure free exploration produces much longer questions while solver performance stops improving. DiagEvo keeps question length stable and improves the mathematical average. (b) Example questions show how unguided self-play increases surface complexity across rounds. (c) DiagEvo uses a hierarchical error-cause memory to guide question generation across rounds.",
                "position": 337
            }
        ]
